---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import caseImageDexcom01 from '../../assets/case-image-dexcom-01.png';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Establishing Dexcom’s European Product Design Studio from Zero"
  summary="Leading an EU-based product design studio at Dexcom, collaborating cross-continentally with global product design leadership across Europe and the US."
  role="Product Design Studio Manager & Senior UX Design Manager"
  timeline="2024 - Present"
  platform="Web & Mobile"
>
  <!-- OVERVIEW -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-2">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 flex-shrink-0 pt-1">
        <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Overview</span>
      </div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Executive summary</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          This case study covers my dual role as <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">Product Design Studio Manager</strong> and
          <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">Senior UX Design Manager at Dexcom</strong>, where I was responsible for establishing and scaling the first Global Product Design presence in Vilnius, Lithuania.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          As the <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">first design hire in the region</strong>, I built a fully functioning, multidisciplinary product design studio and integrated it into Dexcom’s global operating model. Within the first year:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA]">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED] mt-2"></span><span>A <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">10-person studio</strong> was hired, onboarded, and operational</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED] mt-2"></span><span>The studio reached <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">business-as-usual delivery</strong> across multiple global product initiatives</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED] mt-2"></span><span>Vilnius was positioned as <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">Dexcom’s European Product Design hub</strong></span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED] mt-2"></span><span>Strong, ongoing collaboration was established with global leadership across the US and EU</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED] mt-2"></span><span>Studio operations, resourcing, and delivery stabilized without disruption to product timelines</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          The role combines strategic leadership, organizational building, operational oversight, and hands-on people management within a regulated, global health technology environment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SITUATION -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-3">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 flex-shrink-0 pt-1"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Situation</span></div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Context & problem</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          Dexcom was expanding its global footprint and needed to scale product design capacity in Europe while maintaining alignment with its US-based Global Product Design organization.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>No existing design studio, local design leadership, or operational framework in Vilnius</li>
          <li>Global teams required immediate, reliable design capacity</li>
          <li>Organization operated across continents, time zones, and regulated environments</li>
          <li>Design needed tight integration with product, engineering, research, and clinical teams</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">The challenge was not only to hire a team, but to establish a studio that could operate independently while remaining fully embedded in Dexcom’s global product strategy.</p>

        <div class="mt-8">
          <Picture
            src={caseImageDexcom01}
            alt="Dexcom case study - Situation"
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            fallbackFormat="png"
            widths={[472, 944]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 944px, 100vw"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            pictureAttributes={{ class: 'block' }}
            class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/5 shadow-lg"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TASK -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-4">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 flex-shrink-0 pt-1"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Task</span></div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Goals & responsibilities</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          My task was to build, lead, and sustain a high-performing product design studio while simultaneously contributing as a senior leader within the Global Product Design organization.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">Key responsibilities included:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Hire and scale a multidisciplinary design and prototyping team</li>
          <li>Establish studio operations, workflows, and delivery standards</li>
          <li>Onboard the team into Dexcom’s culture, processes, and product ecosystem</li>
          <li>Ensure consistent, high-quality delivery across global initiatives</li>
          <li>Act as a strategic partner to local and global leadership beyond design</li>
          <li>Balance people leadership with organizational and operational accountability</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">This required building trust quickly, both locally and globally, while delivering tangible results from day one.</p>


      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ACTION -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-5">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 flex-shrink-0 pt-1"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Action</span></div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Process & solution</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          I approached the role across three parallel tracks: studio build-up, global integration, and operational excellence.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#EDEDED]">Building the Vilnius design studio</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Hired and scaled a <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">10-person</strong> team, including:
            <ul class="mt-1 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 marker:text-[#787885]">
              <li>UX designers</li>
              <li>UI designers</li>
              <li>Design systems specialists</li>
              <li>Illustrator</li>
              <li>iOS and Android prototyping developers</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>Defined roles, responsibilities, collaboration models, and onboarding frameworks</li>
          <li>Established a strong culture focused on ownership, quality, and collaboration</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#EDEDED] mt-4">Global and cross‑functional integration</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Embedded the studio into Dexcom’s <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">Global Product Design organization</strong></li>
          <li>Partnered closely with senior leaders across:
            <ul class="mt-1 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 marker:text-[#787885]">
              <li>Product management</li>
              <li>Engineering</li>
              <li>Research</li>
              <li>Clinical and regulatory stakeholders</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>Ensured European design efforts aligned with global vision, priorities, and standards</li>
          <li>Acted as a bridge between US and EU teams, aligning expectations, timelines, and delivery models</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#EDEDED] mt-4">Operational leadership and delivery</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Introduced operating rhythms, planning cadences, and resourcing models</li>
          <li>Ensured stable delivery while the studio was still forming</li>
          <li>Balanced short-term execution with long-term organizational development</li>
          <li>Maintained visibility into capacity, risks, and dependencies across initiatives</li>
          <li>Supported designers as both people manager and senior design leader</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          Alongside studio leadership, I continued to operate as a Senior UX Design Manager, contributing to design strategy,
          mentorship, and decision‑making at the global level.
        </p>


      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RESULT -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-6">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 flex-shrink-0 pt-1"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Result</span></div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Outcome & impact</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          The Vilnius Product Design Studio became a stable, trusted, and fully integrated part of Dexcom’s global organization.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA]">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span>Successfully established Dexcom’s <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">first European Product Design studio</strong></span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span>Reached <strong class="text-[#EDEDED]">business-as-usual operations</strong> within the first year</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span>Enabled global teams to scale design capacity without sacrificing quality or speed</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span>Built long‑term partnerships across regions and functions</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span>Created a sustainable operating model for future growth in Europe</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          Most importantly, the studio transitioned from a greenfield initiative into a reliable strategic asset - demonstrating how thoughtful leadership, strong collaboration, and operational rigor can turn a new location into a core part of a global product organization.
        </p>


      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>

